  "summary": "Results inbox worked under RBC-INBOX-01. All 8 items are closed. Each patient was confirmed by name, date of birth and MRN before anything was written to their chart.\n\n1. **Raj Patel (pt-0006), positive FIT.** A GI colonoscopy referral was already active (sr-t2-gi-1020), so per RBC-GI-01 §2 I linked it and did not place a second one. Patient messaged; note written.\n2. **Leslie Parisian (pt-0007), kidney ultrasound.** Simple right kidney cyst. The radiologist recommends no follow-up imaging. Closed with a comment that no follow-up is needed under RBC-INBOX-01 §3; RBC-RAD-05 requires no order.\n3–4. **Edra Ondricka (pt-0016), TSH and lipid panel.** All values normal. Acknowledged and closed.\n5. **Linda Marsh (pt-0013), outside ED CT abdomen/pelvis from 2026-06-04, received this week.** The 5 mm right lower lobe nodule on this scan is the one already followed in lung cancer screening (low-dose chest CT 2025-09-15, Lung-RADS 2). Her yearly screening CT window ended 2026-10-15 with nothing ordered. Per RBC-RAD-05 §2 I ordered the screening CT for 2026-10-23 to 11-06 (sr-t0007), plus a tracking task due 11-06 (task-t0008). Patient messaged; note written.\n6. **Tomás Ruiz (pt-0053, age 16), right knee X-ray.** Aggressive lytic lesion of the lower femur, concerning for a primary bone tumour. Per RBC-RAD-05 §3 I ordered, both urgent and due by 11-05:\n   - MRI of the right femur with and without contrast (sr-t0013)\n   - orthopaedic oncology referral (sr-t0012)\n   Each has a tracking task due 11-05. I gave the ordering NP, Jordan Reyes, an urgent task due today to call his mother/guardian (task-t0014). Note written.\n7. **Walter Brennan (pt-0008), potassium 6.4 on a hemolyzed sample.** Per RBC-LAB-03 §2: urgent repeat metabolic panel by Monday 10-26 (sr-t0020) and a message asking him to come in. On-call was not notified, as the policy says for a hemolyzed sample. Note written.\n8. **Denise Holloway (pt-0010), potassium 6.2, not hemolyzed.** Creatinine rose from 1.46 to 1.58, and lisinopril was started 10-06. Per RBC-LAB-03 §1:\n   - Stat metabolic panel ordered (sr-t0019).\n   - On-call notified at stat priority and asked to call her today and decide whether to hold lisinopril.\n   - Urgent message sent asking her to come in today.\n   - Note written.\n\n**Your attention:**\n- I did not change Ms. Holloway's lisinopril myself; I left that decision to on-call.\n- These are still open:\n  - the guardian call for Tomás Ruiz (Reyes, due today)\n  - on-call's follow-up with Ms. Holloway\n  - the tracking tasks due 11-05 and 11-06\n  - the repeat potassium results for Mr. Brennan and Ms. Holloway, which will need review when they come back",
